{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Fleetwood Mac, Bread and Lesley Gore connect with my recent interest in classic rock, gentle melodies and mid-'60s pop; those musical connections make their collections appealing.",
    "ABBA fits my interest in accessible pop collections, while We Wish You A Merry Christmas feels timely after my recent interest in A Very Special Christmas."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Toby Keith's collection shares the biggest-hits format I often choose, but country does not fit what I want to hear in this session.",
    "I cannot judge The Complete Greatest Hits, The Definitive Collection or The Complete Hit Singles without knowing the artists; a collection title alone does not establish a musical connection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in greatest-hits albums seems to have been treated as enough reason to recommend other hit collections, even when the music may not match.",
    "Several gentle pop choices appeal to me, but that does not mean I would choose them all now; I would pick Bread ahead of Carpenters this time."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The artists and musical styles behind a collection matter more to my choice than words such as greatest, complete or definitive.",
    "My recent Christmas listening gives seasonal music a reason to appeal right now, alongside my longer-running interest in older pop and classic rock."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in older pop and classic-rock collections, but sometimes mistake a shared hits format for a shared musical appeal."
}"}
